# Explore: dynamic single-player free roam (planning/explore.md; owner, 2026-11-16 and 2026-11-17:
# "let me build a character and let me manually use the phone client to explore the world", "Jev
# all the things, make it dynamic"). One player joins with the room code, builds a hero on the
# phone and starts; that hero is the traveller (`@roam`, the id the host passes as DF_RUN_ROAM),
# played from the phone (the seat the host passes as DF_RUN_PLAYER). `@explore on` runs the
# runner's explore loop (play_explore): one open ask a turn, "What do you do?", with cards built
# from the scene the host knows (the people on the plate, a seller's wares, the things worth a close
# look, the ways on below, and a card to keep walking during an approach); the player may always
# type instead. Jev reads every line into one intent (`persona intent`: move, look, talk, trade,
# act, done or clarify, against the scene's ids and the `@way` ids) and the runner hands it to its
# handler; a move toward something on screen walks up to it in steps, each a plate continuing the
# last, the next made ahead. There is no move list and no turn cap: the roam ends when the player
# says they are done. The hero's own kit comes from character creation (no `@inventory`).
@roam explorer
@explore on
@roam_goal You are an adventurer who has just come to this land with no fixed plan, free to wander, look around and meet whoever is there.
@refs max=3
@roam_scene_kind scene
# The ways on: each is a destination named in words (Jev picks the way whose meaning fits the
# line); the words are what the place design is told of the move. They read the same from outside
# a town or inside one.
@way town Go somewhere in or into this town: through its gate from outside, or on to a part of it you have not seen yet.
@way market Make for this town's market or a trading stop to look over the wares, buy what you need or sell what you can spare.
@way road Leave this town by the road and set off toward the next town or landmark along it, one you have not been to yet.
# Walking about: a move by a way shows the sights it passes on the way before its place; a town or
# market move gives the town's look that its places are painted after, and the road leaves it.
@walk road 1 town=leaves
@walk town 2 town=seeds
@walk market 2 town=seeds
@walk_hold 6
# The score follows the roam's tempo (plays only while the toolbar's Music switch is on): explore's
# own table, the painter's day table without its `show` cue.
@tempo_table development/market-threads/explore.music.json
@tempo arrival_road arrive_road 1000
@tempo arrival_town arrive_town 1000
@tempo arrival_market arrive_market 1000
@tempo look look 1000
@tempo walk walk 300
@tempo trade trade 1000
@frames gate=100
@frames every=0
@frames insert_hold=20
# The phone's one ask and the default suggestion of each way; the other cards are the scene's.
@explore_ask What do you do?
@roam_player_card road Take the road | I've seen enough of this place. I'm taking the road on to wherever it leads.
@roam_player_card town Into town | I'll head into town and look around.
@roam_player_card market Find the market | I'll find the market and see what's for sale.
# The player's own hero is the traveller: the persona is written from this hint, and the first
# plate is painted from the hero's reference sheet with this look (no name ever reaches an image).
@roam_hero_hint {name} is a {species} {class} who has just arrived in this land with no fixed plan, free to wander from town to town, look around, trade and talk to whoever they meet.
# The opening plate has no design: it is the active place under this name, and what the hero
# sees on it becomes its things before the first ask.
@roam_start_place the road before the town gate
@roam_start_plate A lone adventurer walks along a dirt road toward the open gate of a walled market town in the morning, fields and a river behind.
